---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Matrix from '../ui/Matrix.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s44b-advanced-caution"
  chapter="Advanced Debugging"
  title="When NOT to Use Invasive Tools"
  notes="Senior engineers only — invasive tools in prod need change control, blast-radius limits, exit plan. tcpdump on production ingress can itself cause an outage. strace high overhead. Chaos engineering validates fixes — staging first. No hypothesis yet, peak traffic, no rollback plan — stop. Exhaust read-only signals first: events, metrics, traces."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <Pill tone="amber">strace / tcpdump</Pill>
      <Pill tone="rose">Chaos Validation</Pill>
    </div>

    <Matrix
      headers={['Technique', 'Proves', 'Prod-safe?']}
      rows={[
        ['kubectl debug (ephemeral)', 'Network, DNS, TLS from pod netns', 'Yes — with RBAC + audit'],
        ['strace -p PID', 'Syscall blocking (I/O, locks)', 'Rarely — high overhead'],
        ['tcpdump -i any port 443', 'Packet reachability, RST, TLS', 'Careful — CPU & capture size'],
        ['Chaos Mesh / Litmus', 'Fix survives kill, partition', 'Staging first, then controlled prod'],
      ]}
    />

    <Callout type="danger">
      When NOT to use invasive tools: no hypothesis yet, peak traffic window, no rollback plan,
      or when read-only signals (events, metrics, traces) haven't been exhausted.
      strace and tcpdump on hot paths can become the incident.
    </Callout>
  </div>
</Slide>
